---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ownershipGuides } from "../data/ownership-guides";
import { comparisonGuides } from "../data/comparison-guides";
import { toThumbnail } from "../utils/images";

const [cars, problems, bestPages] = await Promise.all([
  getCollection("cars"),
  getCollection("problems"),
  getCollection("best")
]);

const flagshipCards = ownershipGuides.slice(0, 3).map((guide) => ({
  href: guide.href,
  title: guide.title,
  description: guide.description,
  eyebrow: guide.eyebrow,
  image: guide.image
}));

const comparisonCards = comparisonGuides.slice(0, 3).map((guide) => ({
  href: guide.href,
  title: guide.title,
  description: guide.description,
  eyebrow: guide.eyebrow,
  image: guide.image
}));

const snapshot = [
  { label: "Cars", value: cars.length, href: "/cars/" },
  { label: "Problem guides", value: problems.length, href: "/problems/" },
  { label: "Best-parts guides", value: bestPages.length, href: "/best/" },
  { label: "Ownership guides", value: ownershipGuides.length, href: "/guides/" },
  { label: "Comparison guides", value: comparisonGuides.length, href: "/comparisons/" },
  { label: "Core vehicles", value: 3, href: "/generations/" }
];
---

<BaseLayout enableAds={false}
  title="Updates"
  description="Recent Kreativ Auto improvements, including new ownership guides, better browsing, stronger fitment notes, and clearer repair checks."
>
  <div class="container-shell py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="surface hero-frame p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.15fr_0.85fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Updates</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">Recent Kreativ Auto improvements</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-steel">
            A simple record of meaningful changes: new ownership checks, better diagnosis flow, improved part comparisons, and cleaner navigation.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-steel">
            For the best current starting points, use the ownership guides, comparison guides, and generation views for Civic, RAV4, and Tiguan.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="accent-panel p-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">Current snapshot</p>
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {snapshot.map((item) => (
              <a
                class="snapshot-card p-4"
                href={item.href}
                data-ka-event="updates_snapshot_click"
                data-ka-section="updates_snapshot"
                data-ka-label={item.label}
              >
                <p class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">{item.value}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-steel">{item.label}</p>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 surface hero-frame p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Most useful recent improvements</h2>
          <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">More ownership checks</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                Added common-problem, maintenance-cost, pre-purchase, what-to-avoid, and trim-choice guidance for the most researched vehicles.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Faster browsing</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                Filters and clearer navigation make it easier to move by vehicle, symptom, part category, or powertrain.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="editorial-card">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Better buying signals</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
                Part guides now have tighter product links, clearer buying tiers, better imagery, and stronger first-check guidance before a repair turns into a parts order.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-4">
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/guides/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Ownership</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Open ownership guides</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Start with broader ownership, maintenance, and buying checks before narrowing into a single repair.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/comparisons/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Comparisons</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Open comparison guides</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Use drivetrain, engine, hybrid, and facelift comparisons where one symptom or one part is too narrow.</p>
          </a>
          <a class="mesh-card p-5 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5" href="/generations/volkswagen-tiguan-tiguan-ii-facelift-2020-2024/">
            <p class="eyebrow">Generation</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Open the Tiguan generation</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Use the Tiguan II facelift view when year, trim, and drivetrain details change the repair or buying advice.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Flagship Guides</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Cornerstone guides added recently</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {flagshipCards.map((card) => (
          <a class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-white" href={card.href}>
            {card.image && (
              <div class="image-frame image-frame-card">
                <img
                  src={toThumbnail(card.image)}
                  alt={card.title}
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  width="960"
                  height="640"
                />
              </div>
            )}
            <div class="p-5">
              <p class="eyebrow">{card.eyebrow}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{card.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">{card.description}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 surface p-6 sm:p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow">Comparison Guides</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">High-value version guides</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {comparisonCards.map((card) => (
          <a class="mesh-card overflow-hidden p-0 transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-white" href={card.href}>
            {card.image && (
              <div class="image-frame image-frame-card">
                <img
                  src={toThumbnail(card.image)}
                  alt={card.title}
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  width="960"
                  height="640"
                />
              </div>
            )}
            <div class="p-5">
              <p class="eyebrow">{card.eyebrow}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{card.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">{card.description}</p>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">May 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">More models received practical checks</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Refreshed the 2020 Honda Accord, 2020 Mazda 3, and 2020 Toyota Corolla vehicle guides with cleaner imagery and clearer links into problem, parts, and ownership checks.</li>
          <li>Added a 2020 Honda Accord common-problems cornerstone guide covering weak A/C at idle, brake vibration, battery behavior, and front-end noise.</li>
          <li>Added a 2020 Mazda 3 common-problems cornerstone guide covering front-end clunks, brake noise, road hum, and short-trip battery behavior.</li>
          <li>Added a 2020 Toyota Corolla maintenance-costs and weak-points guide to tie Corolla repair examples to ownership-cost planning.</li>
          <li>Added maintenance-costs and weak-points guides for the 2020 Honda Accord and 2020 Mazda 3.</li>
          <li>Added a 2020 Toyota Camry common-problems cornerstone guide covering brake squeal, highway vibration, battery behavior, and road-noise diagnosis.</li>
          <li>Added common-problems coverage for the 2020 Honda CR-V and 2020 Mazda CX-5, including battery, brake, suspension, and road-noise checks.</li>
          <li>Added what-to-avoid guides for the 2020 Honda Accord, 2020 Mazda 3, and 2020 Toyota Corolla.</li>
          <li>Improved second-tier guide imagery for Accord, Mazda 3, and Corolla, and added a repo health check for Dropbox conflict files and broken image references.</li>
          <li>Added first-pass ownership checks for Audi Q5, BMW 3 Series, Ford F-150, Mercedes-Benz C-Class, Subaru Outback, and VW Golf GTI.</li>
          <li>Replaced the remaining SVG vehicle visuals for Accord, Mazda 3, and Corolla with raster JPEG assets and matching thumbnails.</li>
          <li>Strengthened problem-page triage blocks with can-you-drive, cost-range, and DIY-difficulty decision cards across all problem guides.</li>
          <li>Hardened the manual daily maintenance workflow with repo health checks before direct pushes.</li>
          <li>Connected the new guides to the matching vehicles, generations, and repair topics.</li>
          <li>Added weekly planning and daily maintenance checks to catch missing images, stale dates, broken references, and thin draft language earlier.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">April 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Ownership and comparison guidance expanded</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Expanded Civic, RAV4, and Tiguan with more problem guides, best-parts guides, and clearer links between diagnosis, parts, and ownership checks.</li>
          <li>Added common-problems, maintenance, pre-purchase, what-to-avoid, and trim-buying guides for the three core vehicles.</li>
          <li>Improved generation views with common trouble spots, first parts to check, trim and year caveats, visual highlights, and clearer next-read paths.</li>
          <li>Moved comparisons into a dedicated public section and kept the old tools paths as redirects.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest problem guides with quick verdicts, first checks, confusion points, and clearer signs that a car should not keep being driven.</li>
          <li>Improved the strongest best-parts guides with clearer buying tiers, stronger “best for” and “avoid if” logic, and tighter product-link quality.</li>
          <li>Added more branded and better-matched part imagery, generated thumbnails for faster browsing, and converted heavier hero images to lighter web formats.</li>
          <li>Improved the design system with stronger guide treatment, denser image coverage, better typography, and clearer editorial hierarchy.</li>
          <li>Added browse filters so visitors can narrow by vehicle, guide type, category, and symptom area.</li>
          <li>Refreshed trust pages, added a favicon, and cleaned up public navigation.</li>
          <li>Added weekly planning and daily maintenance checks to catch missing images, stale dates, broken references, and thin draft language earlier.</li>
          <li>Added common-problems cornerstone guides for the 2020 Honda CR-V, 2020 Mazda CX-5, and 2020 Toyota Corolla.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
        <p class="eyebrow">March 2026</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Launch version</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-steel marker:text-accent">
          <li>Launched the first public version of Kreativ Auto with vehicle guides, problem guides, and best-parts guides for common maintenance and repair decisions.</li>
          <li>Added browse paths for brands, models, generations, and part categories so it is easier to jump from one vehicle or repair topic to the next.</li>
          <li>Expanded the homepage with featured cars, common problems, and parts guides to help visitors reach useful pages faster.</li>
          <li>Reworked the writing to make problem symptoms, likely causes, and repair options clearer and easier to scan.</li>
          <li>Added real car and parts photos across key guides to make Kreativ Auto more visual and easier to browse.</li>
          <li>Published About, Affiliate Disclosure, Editorial Policy, and Contact pages so readers can better understand how recommendations are made.</li>
          <li>Improved search visibility with sitemap support, crawl guidance, breadcrumbs, and structured data.</li>
          <li>Brought Kreativ Auto live on its public domain.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
